*.tsbuildinfo

# `dist/` is NOT ignored for the two published packages (@arthome/core and
#   @arthome/contracts): their .d.ts files are tracked deliberately, against the
#   usual practice, because that is what makes a contract change visible in a
#   review rather than in an incident at a consumer.
#   See architecture/code-conventions.md section 2.4, gate 8.
#   (git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so we exclude
#   `dist/` only where it really is an artefact.)
#
#   BUT ONLY THE `.d.ts`. The reason above is "a contract change visible in a
#   REVIEW", and that reason covers the declarations and nothing else:
#     - a `.d.ts.map` is Base64 VLQ. It is unreadable, it regenerates on every
#       build, and it DEFEATS the stated purpose — a one-line contract change
#       arrives buried under a hundred lines of mapping;
#     - a `.js` in dist duplicates a source file sitting in the same repository,
#       where a reviewer can read it better.
#   122 of 244 tracked dist files were maps before this line existed.
#
#   What SHIPS is built at publish time; what is TRACKED is what a reviewer
#   reads. Those are different sets, and tracking `dist/` wholesale conflated
#   them. `declarationMap` and `sourceMap` stay on in lib.json — the maps are
#   still produced and still published, they are just not committed.
/dist/
packages/tooling/dist/
tools/*/dist/
packages/*/dist/**/*.map
packages/*/dist/**/*.js

# Extraction scratch from the OpenAPI translation harness (backend-contracts).
# Regenerated on demand; 140 KB of French source units, not a deliverable.
*.units.json

# Python bytecode, created by importing a tools/ gate as a module while testing it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
packages/tooling/docs/
